Z||000000||David DeVoe||11-21-2001||12:52 AM||||Is it just me or do others experience problems with after market parts. I just don't seem to get the life out of parts that I think I should. I'd hate to think that it was just bad luck on my part.<BR>Dave<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||11-21-2001||01:21 AM||||Well...I purchased the FieroStore clutch master cylinder.  It didn't work good at all.  Couldn't get the clutch to work.  I ordered the factory part and now it works fine.  Have had similar experiences with aftermarket parts, this one just happens to be recent.  I am just going to buy GM from now on!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||11-21-2001||01:51 AM||||I put on 4 AutoZone reman alternators in 2 months last summer. The last one seems to be holding up. <P>BTW, David. <P>The stuff went out this afternoon. I just got back in town. Sorry about the delay.  <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Banzai||11-21-2001||06:11 AM||||In my experience some aftermarket parts are better than others. Chassis parts-- stick with MOOG.  Electrics (alternator/starter) GM/AcDelco is the best. You take a chance on any rebuilt electronics. Some are better than others. Sensors etc.-- AcDelco again is the best. There are definately visable differences in OEM and aftermarket parts. <P>I am completing a resto on an 84' SE and have replaced all the suspension and driveline components. I was amazed at the difference in some of the parts.<P>Dave, it's good to see another member in the immediate area. I should have my car road worthy by tonight. I have to drill and tap the front swaybar mounting holes as all four bolts snapped off during disassembly. After that I have to bleed the brakes. If it's dry out-----I WILL BE TAKING MY BABY FOR A SPIN TONIGHT WOOOOOOOO HOOOOOOOO. Maybe we can get together before the snow flys.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>"I promise Honey, it'll be done in one MORE week----------"||||reg||1
Z||000004||revin||11-21-2001||07:17 AM||||I just got a slave cyl. from these guys. Local $165- them   $ 90. Real GM parts  <A HREF="http://www.GMPartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.GMPartsdirect.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||11-21-2001||09:25 AM||||Well, I just had to replace the rebuilt alt. on my Formula (don't know what brand, came with the car).  I got a 105 amp rebuilt model from NAPA for $139.  A bit more than the AutoZone rebuild, but it comes not only with a Lifetime warranty, but 24hr. roadside and towing service if the alternator fails.  So a free tow (within 25miles) to my service center (my driveway) if the alt. craps out is pretty good peice of mind.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick's Dad||11-21-2001||04:27 PM||||Mixed results:<P>KYB Shocks and Struts, (unknown) springs, and Carbomet brake pads for my 88 Formula from Fiero Store: No problems at all. Lotsa fun.<P>Exhaust system from crossover pipe back from IRM: Mostly good. Larger Cat and 2½" pipes are still intact, but Hooker resonater tips (twin duals) have rotted off the ends.<P>Also OK: underdrive pulley, K&N filter, Fiero Store rebuilt steering rack.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||11-21-2001||04:39 PM||||The aftermarket has allways been a mixed bag and always will be.<P>One thing I've learned... make sure you get the "lifetime" versions of things like alternators and whatever else. The "1 year" ones aren't likely to last even the year.<P>Borg Warner (AKA BWD) has sensors and allot of other things that are at least as good as AC/Delco. I've got 25,000 miles on a set of their plug wires. They are the only source of sensors and ignition modules I trust besides OE.<P>Bosch for O2 sensors. they invented the damn things after all.<P>Accel has gone to hell in the last year or three. Their DIS coils were complete trash.<P>Magnecor has some of the best plug wires on the planet. I'll be going back to those on my DIS motor. couldn't aford them last time I needed wires, plus I needed them same day.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Spektrum-87GT||11-21-2001||09:25 PM||||i've got an aftermarket steering rack... feels fine to me<P>definitily worth the 500 bucks i saved!!!||||reg||1
